  "articlePanels": [
    {
      "kind": "lede",
      "html": "<p>Report software is often made for warm offices. It assumes dry hands and good light. Real sites are not like that. Speaking suits real sites.</p>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "takeaways",
      "heading": "The short version",
      "html": "<ul><li>Speaking beats typing on site, most of all in gloves.</li><li>Voice notes made during the job give truer records than entries typed from memory hours later.</li><li>Spoken notes hold more detail than typed notes written in a rush.</li><li>Quickler works in WhatsApp. Use the microphone button. No new tool to learn.</li><li>The final report is written text. It looks the same whether you spoke or typed.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "default",
      "eyebrow": "The options",
      "heading": "Ways to turn voice notes into a report",
      "html": "<p>I make Quickler, so read this with that in mind. Every line about another tool comes from its own website, checked on 18 November 2026. Where I could not check something, I leave it out.</p><ul><li><strong>Phone dictation</strong> (<a href=\"https://support.apple.com/en-gb/guide/iphone/iph2c0651d2/ios\" rel=\"noopener\">built into iPhone and Android keyboards</a>). Free. Speak and the words appear as text. You still move them into your report and match the photos. <em>Better when:</em> you write few reports and want no new tool.</li><li><strong>Sitemate</strong> (<a href=\"https://sitemate.com/use-cases/safety-inspection\" rel=\"noopener\">sitemate.com</a>). Record voice observations and photos on the walk; AI sorts them into hazard descriptions and drafts the safety report for you to approve. <em>Better when:</em> you run construction or civil sites.</li><li><strong>Fieldvox</strong> (<a href=\"https://fieldvox.app/\" rel=\"noopener\">fieldvox.app</a>). An iPhone app: photograph an issue, mark it up, speak a note, and it writes the title, comment, assignee and due date into a PDF report. <em>Better when:</em> you produce snagging or defect lists on an iPhone.</li><li><strong>Fire Record</strong> (<a href=\"https://firerecord.co.uk/\" rel=\"noopener\">firerecord.co.uk</a>). For UK fire risk assessors: walk, talk and take photos on your phone, and it drafts the full report to PAS 79-1:2020 or BS 9792:2025. <em>Better when:</em> you write fire risk assessments.</li><li><strong>Quickler</strong> (<a href=\"/pages/how-it-works.html\">how it works</a>). Send voice notes, text or photos in WhatsApp as you walk. Each voice note is written out, saved as the answer to the right question, and your own Word or PDF report is filled. <em>Better when:</em> you have your own report layout and want any kind of inspection written up from what you said.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "default",
