    {
      "kind": "default",
      "eyebrow": "Honest records",
      "heading": "Why spoken records are easier to defend",
      "html": "<p>When you type, you know you are writing a document. That invites tidying. Borderline becomes \"within tolerance\". Doubt disappears.</p><p>Speaking feels less formal, so you say it as it is. \"Tread's getting close, I'd say 3mm, worth watching.\" \"Could not see the flue terminal from the ground, look closer next visit.\"</p><p>In an insurance claim or a review, a record that states a borderline finding honestly is stronger than one tidied to say \"satisfactory\".</p>"
