      "html": "<h3>How do I turn voice notes into an inspection report?</h3><p>Dictate and paste the text yourself, use an app that drafts a report from your voice notes, or send them in WhatsApp to Quickler, which writes them out and fills your own report.</p><h3>Can I send voice notes instead of typing my inspection?</h3><p>Yes, if the tool writes them out. In Quickler each voice note is written out and saved as text against the question, so the report reads as a normal written record.</p><h3>Can I use voice notes for site reports in the UK?</h3><p>A voice recording alone is not a written record. In Quickler each voice note is written out and saved as text against the right question. The final report is written text.</p><h3>How well does it handle technical words?</h3><p>Common trade words come out well. You may need a quick correction for unusual phrasing. You can fix any word before you send the report.</p><h3>Does typing in gloves cause errors?</h3><p>Yes. Touchscreens often miss gloved input. Cold hands type slowly and badly. People type the least they can, so the record is thin.</p><h3>What happens to my voice notes?</h3><p>They are written out and saved as text against the right question. You do not need to retype them. The final report holds the written text.</p><h3>Related guides</h3><ul><li><a href=\"/pages/how-to-write-site-inspection-report-uk.html\">How to write a site inspection report</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/paperless-inspections-uk-trades.html\">Paperless inspections for UK trades</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/uk-field-compliance-reporting-guide.html\">UK field compliance reporting guide</a></li></ul>"
